tarring the Radio City Rockettes. In addition, it engages in the entertainment and sports bookings business that showcase a range of concerts, family shows, and special events, as well as various sporting events. The company was formerly known as MSGE Spinco, Inc. Madison Square Garden Entertainment Corp. was incorporated in 2022 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James Lawrence Dolan | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $5.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the above the sector median among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $305K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $31K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Madison Square Garden Entertain is a mid-cap communication services business with a $3.7B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $323M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.31\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber"